Z||000007||DRH||04-25-2001||04:56 PM||||To add to the list of why NOT to do it...<P>I suspect the shape of the tunnel adds quite of bit of strength to the unibody design. Think of the strength of a big piece of c-channel compared to flat sheet metal.||||reg||1
Z||000008||EdsB52||04-25-2001||06:15 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B>To add to the list of why NOT to do it...<P>I suspect the shape of the tunnel adds quite of bit of strength to the unibody design. Think of the strength of a big piece of c-channel compared to flat sheet metal.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>You're right, but that does not add to the list of why not to do it, as I have already addressed that issue. Although you stated it much more eliquintly <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||EdsB52||04-25-2001||06:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Ken Wittlief:<BR><B>Does your car have a luggage rack, or a wing? Strapping a beer keg on the luggage rack and using it for a fuel tank, that would look cool<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ya, and you could eliminate the need for a fuel pump. When you start it up in the morning and periodically throughout the day, you'd just have to go back and give it a couple of pumps. You have gravity plus a little pressure. Hey, if the Fiero Store or someone is reading, me and Ken hereby apply for a patent on this idea and demand royalties if replicated <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Tryxalon||04-25-2001||09:04 PM||||I would love to reply to this question ... <P>but ....<P><BR><B> I'm laughing too hard!!! </B> <P>||||reg||10
Z||000011||fyerstarter||04-25-2001||09:25 PM||||I think this would have to go in my list of useless mods that people think up to do to their car, probably while sitting on the can one afternoon with nothing else to do.<P>I think the basic idea with a mid-engine car is to get most of the weight centered between all 4 wheels. Right where the gas tank is now. If anything the Fiero needs more weight up front and less out back, thus the battery in the front compartment mod.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Spektyr||04-25-2001||10:19 PM||||My sister freaked out when I told her where the gas tank was in my Fiero.<P>"Aren't you afraid to be sitting that close to it?"<P>"Well, look at it this way... do you think I'll survive the impact that crushes the gas tank?"<P>"Uh, probably not."<P>"So why would I care if I'm on fire?"<P>------------------<BR>85 GT (to be modified...)<BR>--Um, no the paint isn't oxidized, that's the ultra-rare Whirlpool White textured finish... yeah.<BR>89 Lincoln Town Car (has Fiero Envy)<BR>--Hey!  Can I have an anti-sway bar too?||||reg||1
Z||000013||dman||04-26-2001||07:22 AM||||Hello Gabriel.<P>Lots of folks have expressed their thoughts and opinions as to why a gas tank relocation is not a good thing. Many good points have been raised (as well as a bit of poo-poo-ing and nay-saying).<P>I'd like to try and answer your question. Some replica builders have done exactly what you've described. The gas tank is relocated (actually it is removed and a fuel cell is placed where the spare tire used to be). You are absolutely correct about reinforcing the area once occupied by the original tank. For the replicar builders, reinforcing the entire car (not just because of the gas tank removal) is a standard operation since the Fiero is pretty much chopped up.<P>Note: What I'm describing is not often done and only by those individuals who possess excellent fabrication skills. When these (quality) replicars are completed, the craftsmanship often exceeds that found in many factory built automobiles. I've helped restore an authentic Lamborghini Diablo and I can tell you that some replica Diablo's are actually better built (construction wise but not necessarily technology). Unfortunately this type of extreme attention to detail is rather rare, very few of these cars are actually ever seen. In fact they are often mistaken for the authentic item.<P>Hopefully I will not be attacked for answering your question. If anyone happens to find my reply difficult to accept or even blasphemous that's just fine by me; everyone is entitled to an opinion. Just don't give me crap about it. I'm just answering a question. I don't feel like I should have to justify myself but the forum hasn't been as friendly as it once was.<P>Peace, and happy Fiero-ing.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000014||EdsB52||04-26-2001||10:09 AM||||Come on everyone, let's lynch dman! He's screwing up a perfectly good chance to satire someone's ridiculous post! <P><BR>Just kidding. We all have daydreams about doing stupid things to our Fieros, when we actually barely have time to post them so we get laughed at. I've even thought it would be unique to make a front engine Fiero. Put a V-8 or V-6 up there, move the gas tank, and put a straight axle in the back. It wouldn't make for a better car, just a more unique car because I would be the one stupid enough to waste a year of my life doing it. If anyone ever does relocate the gas tank, for whatever reason, I hope they are 19 yo with nothing to their name because if you modify a federally (DOT) approved motor vehicle, sell it, and have someone wreck it, you'll be driving nothing more than a 1984 Fiero with 178,000 miles on it (you'll be sued)!<p>[This message has been edited by EdsB52 (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||gabriel||04-26-2001||01:12 PM||||Wow!<P>  Gee, what responses!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P> Okay, okay, let me elaborate:<P>This is  for a replicar project, exactly as Dman stated. (and I thank you for that answer, Dman.)<P>  The 85 Fiero donor is being converted to a Ferrari 512 Testarossa clone.  Most of the work has already been done, including the 7.5 inch frame stretch & the longitudial SHO engine/Porsche transaxle mounting as well as the roof & window mods. The custom shifter & clutch setup I fabricated myself & already takes into account the loss of tunnel space.<BR>I'm now working on fabricating a custom exhaust/header setup/<BR> I've posted pics to the forum on this project already.<BR> To be accurate, the tunnel must go, and that is the reason for the (not useless)question & the (not ridiculous) post.  <P> As for the gas tank in the rear being unsafe, I think that's where most tanks are on American cars. (abiet they don't have the engine back there)  However I was also thinking of a frontal location to improve weight distribution even further; maybe using fuel cells, maybe not. <P>  The question of the details of stiffening the frame remains ... <p>[This message has been edited by gabriel (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000016||Carrolles||04-26-2001||02:19 PM||||I believe no question or idea is stupid. Some may make more sense than others.<P>Sometimes its easy to forget that most of us have never met personnaly and we treat each other like we've been buddies forever, consequently we sometimes seem insensitive and make wise cracks that seem inappropriate to newcomers.  No harm intended.<P>Your project sounds interesting and you obviously have talent and ambition for the task.  I'd like to see the pics you posted.  Where can I see them?<P>Good luck and keep us posted on your progress.<P>Carroll||||reg||1
Z||000017||gabriel||04-26-2001||07:39 PM||||&gt;I'd like to see the pics you posted. Where can I see them?<P>Here:   <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008880.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/008880.html</A> <P>Thank you - gabriel||||reg||1
Z||000018||Fierowrecker||04-26-2001||09:00 PM||||Hey Gabe!<BR>Been thinking along the same lines, myself...<BR>Don't take the negative comments to heart, the Wright bro's took a lot of heat before they flew...<BR>Personally, I want to locate the seat to a central location, along with steering and such...<BR>Kinda like a go kart...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000019||gabriel||04-27-2001||11:06 AM||||&gt;Don't take the negative comments to heart<P>Hey, I didn't.  <P>  Just restating my case  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Still, I believe that some in the forum have reinforced the space frame, & I was looking for some input as to how they , or others, had done that.  No need to reinvent the wheel, after all.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
